{'translated_term': 'Tsala Tsa Lomelo ya Pabili', 
'translation_rationale': 'The Swati language uses a combination of prefixes, suffixes, and root words to convey meaning. In this case, "Tsala" means community or public, "Tsa" is a possessive marker indicating ownership, "Lomelo" means place or space, and "ya Pabili" indicates the nature of the space as being for or related to people or the public. This translation aims to capture the essence of Public History in Swati, conveying it as a communal or public space for historical inquiry and reflection.', 
